# Latin/Greek/Cyrillic coverage for the LIVE session itself — the installer's
# own language picker lists Русский, 日本語, العربية, and dejavu draws none of
# them, so the menu offering them rendered as boxes. noto-fonts is ~10MB and
# covers everything except CJK/Indic, which the installer pulls per-language
# (noto-fonts-cjk alone is ~130MB, too much to put on every ISO).
#
# This also makes the compositor honest elsewhere: a filename or an RSS headline
# in a script dejavu lacks drew as boxes on the live ISO, whatever the locale.
noto-fonts
wlroots0.20
# wlr_scene fork giving synui blur + rounded corners. Built by build.sh into
# local-repo; listed explicitly (like wlroots0.20) rather than left to synui's
# dependency resolution, since it exists in no upstream repo. The 0.5 line is
# the one built against wlroots 0.20 — the pair synui links today.
scenefx0.5
librsvg
plymouth
archiso
mkinitcpio-archiso
syslinux
# The CPU llama build, named explicitly. The repo also carries
# synapse-llama-cuda, which provides+conflicts synapse-llama — naming the one we
# want here means the ISO's dependency resolution can never fall through to the
# CUDA provider, whose libs NEED libcuda.so.1 at load and would make synapd fail
# to start on every machine without an NVIDIA driver. The GPU build is for
# installed systems (syn-install picks it when it sees the hardware), never here.
synapse-llama
synapd
synsh
synnet
synguard
synui
syn-model
syn
syn-firstboot
syn-install
syn-update
synapse_kmod
nexus-chat
tepris
chibi
vibe
foot
kitty
# Application launcher on Super+Space. rofi 2.0.0 merged lbonn's Wayland port
# into mainline, so this is the plain `rofi` package (it Provides/Replaces
# rofi-wayland) talking layer-shell to synui — no XWayland, no AUR, no fork.
#
# It does NOT replace the cmdbar, which is native and carries the synsh intents
# and output capture; that moved to Super+= (see seed_default_binds in
# synui/src/config.c). rofi is the plain "launch an app" key.
#
# Two Wayland-backend limitations upstream documents in the 2.0.0 notes: it
# cannot detect clicks outside its own surface, so clicking away does not
# dismiss it (Escape does), and it flickers on startup because scale is
# detected late.
rofi
firefox
# File manager. Pulls Qt6 + KF6 (~550MB), which is why synui ships the two
# /etc/xdg files KDE-outside-Plasma needs to actually work: menus/applications.menu
# (or every file opens the "Open With" chooser) and kdeglobals (or "Open Terminal"
# silently does nothing, KIO's fallback being a konsole we don't ship).
dolphin
# Phone pairing: notifications, file transfer, clipboard, remote control.
# Costs almost nothing on top of dolphin — the KF6 tree is already paid for by
# the line above — and the parts that would normally need theming work are
# already SynapseOS's: the phone's notifications go through knotifications to
# org.freedesktop.Notifications, which synui itself serves and draws, and the
# indicator is a StatusNotifierItem, which the quickshell bar already hosts.
#
# The daemon is what has to be running for a phone to reach the desktop, and
# the /etc/xdg/autostart file the package ships for it is DEAD HERE: nothing in
# a synui session implements the XDG autostart spec (synui's autostart is
# synuirc `autostart =` lines). /etc/synui/synuirc starts the indicator, which
# D-Bus-activates the daemon and supplies the tray icon in one go.
kdeconnect
gamescope
# The bar. Neither of these was on the ISO, so the live session had no bar at
# all — no clock, no tray, no network indicator — while an installed system had
# one; that was an oversight, not a decision. synui pulls quickshell in as a
# dependency now, but list it explicitly: what the ISO ships should be readable
# here rather than inferred from someone else's depends. wtype is how the bar's
# SYNAPSE button asks synui to open the start menu (there is no other IPC in).
#
# quickshell replaced waybar as the bar on 2026-07-24 (synui/systemd/synui-bar.sh
# records why). waybar is deliberately absent: nothing starts it, and the ISO is
# already ~7GB.
quickshell
wtype

# Screen recording (Super+Shift+R). synui pulls it in as a dependency; listed
# here so what the ISO ships is readable rather than inferred.
wf-recorder

# Printing. SynapseOS shipped Dolphin and Firefox and no way to print from
# either. cups brings its own web admin UI on localhost:631, so there is no
# printer-setup GUI to write or ship — the start menu just opens it.
#
# cups pulls avahi itself, which is most of what makes this work: a printer made
# since ~2015 speaks IPP Everywhere / AirPrint, so cups discovers it over mDNS
# and prints with no driver at all. nss-mdns is the glibc half of that — without
# it nothing resolves the printer's own .local name. ghostscript is what renders
# PDF for printers that don't do it themselves; cups-pdf adds a "Print to PDF"
# printer, which is the one every machine should have.
cups
cups-pdf
ghostscript
nss-mdns
# The driverless-IPP story above covers any printer since ~2015. The Xpress
# M2020W predates it: an SPL device cups cannot drive without Samsung's ULD
# rastertospl filter. samsung-m2020 (built from samsung-m2020/PKGBUILD) ships
# it so the live ISO — not just installed disks — can print to one.
samsung-m2020

# Shelly — a GTK4 + libalpm package manager (CLI `shelly`, GUI `shelly-ui`), a
# friendlier front-end to pacman/AUR/Flatpak. Built from shelly/PKGBUILD as
# the pkgname `shelly-bin` (it provides `shelly`); listed by exact name so
# pacstrap never has to resolve the provider.
shelly-bin

# Bluetooth. bluez is the daemon (org.bluez); bluez-utils is bluetoothctl, which
# synui does not need — it talks BlueZ over sd-bus itself (synui/src/bt.c) — but
# which is the only way to debug a radio from a shell when the panel says no.
bluez
bluez-utils

# Wine so the live environment can run Windows .exe/.msi, and so the packages
# are cached on the ISO for the installer's pacstrap (syn-install adds them to
# the target). wine-mono covers .NET-based installers.
wine
wine-mono
virtualbox-guest-utils
dkms
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
slurp
grim
rtkit

# Wallpaper Engine backgrounds (the Workshop rows in synui's Super+W picker,
# driven by the synui-wpengine script this package also ships). Built from
# linux-wallpaperengine-pkg/PKGBUILD against a pinned upstream commit; it is in
# no pacman repo, so pacstrap can only get it from our local-repo.
#
# synui does NOT depend on it — the picker simply shows no Workshop rows when
# it is absent — so this line is the only thing putting it on the ISO. It is
# listed rather than left off because the wallpapers come from Steam Workshop
# subscriptions, and a user who has just subscribed to one should not then have
# to build a CEF-carrying package by hand to see it.
linux-wallpaperengine
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs
f2fs-tools
snapper
snap-pac
grub-btrfs
inotify-tools
limine
limine-snapper-sync
zram-generator
